node_modules/

# The build output. Committed only on a release, as a release asset: a bundle in every
# commit makes every diff twice as long and the second half unreadable.
#
# Anchored to the root. Written as `main.js` it matched every file of that name at any
# depth, which silently excluded src/main.js, the plugin's own entry point, from the
# repository. Everything still built here because the file was on disk; a clean clone
# could not build at all, and nobody noticed until the directory's review tried.
/main.js

# Whatever vault this is being tested against.
test-vault/
